"The phrase \"Five Elements\" — wood, fire, earth, metal, and water — sounds, to an English speaker, like an ancient and mistaken attempt at chemistry, the way early Greek thinkers once proposed that everything was made of four elements. Chinese medicine is not making a claim about chemistry at all. The five elements are a classification system, a way of sorting phenomena — organs, seasons, emotions, colors, tastes, even sounds — into five families based on shared patterns of behavior, not shared physical substance.": "2c1c58d5a6d1",
"The phrase \"Five Elements\" — wood, fire, earth, metal, and water — sounds, to an English speaker, like an ancient and mistaken attempt at chemistry, the way early Greek thinkers once proposed that everything was made of four elements. Chinese medicine is not making a claim about chemistry at all. The five elements are a classification system, a way of sorting phenomena — organs, seasons, emotions, colors, tastes, even sounds — into five families based on shared patterns of behavior, not shared physical substance. Wood describes things associated with growth, flexibility, and upward movement — spring, the color green, the emotion of anger, a shoot pushing through soil. Fire describes things associated with heat, activity, and rising — summer, the color red, joy, a flame reaching upward. Earth describes things associated with stability, nourishment, and centering — late summer, the color yellow, worry, soil that holds and feeds a plant's roots. Metal describes things associated with contraction, clarity, and letting go — autumn, the color white, grief, a blade that cuts cleanly. Water describes things associated with stillness, storage, and downward movement — winter, the color black, fear, water pooling at the lowest point. None of these five categories describes a physical ingredient inside the body. They describe a pattern — the same way saying someone has a \"fiery temper\" doesn't mean flames are involved. Once the five elements are read as five patterns rather than five materials, the rest of the system stops sounding mystical and starts sounding like what it actually is: an organizing chart for how different parts of a person, and different parts of nature, tend to behave.": "588f67d02978",
